  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The current best (config_013, 0.7250) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. The largest remaining uncertainty is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000 has never been tested in any completed experiment. config_019 isolates this variable by pairing pca_n2000 with the known-best architecture (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted), directly testing whether a high-dimensional linear encoder can match or exceed the nonlinear scVI encoder. If pca_n2000 performs comparably, it would be a cheaper encoder to build on; if it underperforms significantly, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and the remaining 2 experiments should focus on fine-tuning around the scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted + imagenet_vit_l core. This is the highest-information experiment available: it reduces uncertainty on the single most impactful untested design axis while keeping the rest of the architecture at proven-optimal settings. Expected cost is moderate (~3–3.5 GPU hours), slightly below config_013's 3.60 since PCA projection is cheaper than scVI encoding, with the transformer aggregation and ViT-L image backbone dominating runtime."
}

